# The Mikron HSM 400U retrofit (machine/hsm400u.mill: five simulated drives,
# the B/C trunnion through xyzbc-trt-kins): a tool-centre-point move turns
# the table (B 0 -> 30, C 0 -> 90) while X Y Z keep the tool tip on its
# point of the work, 50 mm above the pallet; then a five-axis line. The tip,
# judged in the work's frame (the inverse kinematics of the simulated table
# angles and tool), stays within a few um; B holds against its unbalance at
# 90 deg.
@program mill/mill_sim
@args mill/machine/hsm400u.mill
@timeout 300
lcnc 1
run 0.3
move 2.5 230 180 -300 0 0
run 0.4
print wx wy wz
mark
rtcp 3 30 90
run 0.3
print fault hits max_ework max_econtw ework tb tc wx wy wz
mark
wmove 2 250 180 -300 20 150
run 0.3
print fault max_econtw ework wx
move 4 200 160 -150 90 150
run 0.5
mark
run 1
print fault max_ferr_b tb
@expect mill.wx[1] ~ 230 0.01
@expect mill.wy[1] ~ 180 0.01
@expect max mill.fault == 0
@expect mill.hits == 0
@expect mill.max_ework[1] < 10
@expect mill.max_econtw[1] < 10
@expect mill.ework[1] < 3
@expect mill.tb[1] ~ 30 0.01
@expect mill.tc[1] ~ 90 0.01
@expect mill.wx[2] ~ 230 0.005
@expect mill.wy[2] ~ 180 0.005
@expect mill.wz[2] ~ -300 0.005
@expect mill.max_econtw[2] < 15
@expect mill.wx[3] ~ 250 0.005
@expect mill.max_ferr_b < 5
@expect mill.tb[2] ~ 90 0.01
